# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Fixture templates and binaries are byte-content, not source.
#
# Git's text normalisation (core.autocrlf, text=auto, eol=) can silently
# convert CRLF↔LF or strip a final newline on checkout. The staging tests
# assert byte-identity against the fixture, so *any* normalisation breaks
# them in a way that depends on the developer's git configuration — the
# worst kind of failure: it works on your machine and fails in CI.
#
# -text disables all text normalisation for these paths.
# -diff disables line-oriented diff (a binary diff is correct for a
# template whose bytes are the contract; a line diff is misleading).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
tests/fixtures/**/*.j2  -text -diff
tests/fixtures/**/*.png -text -diff
